# Security Guidelines

## Authentication

- Implement proper JWT handling
- Use secure cookie storage
- Implement proper logout functionality
- Use refresh tokens for long-term sessions
- Implement rate limiting for auth endpoints

## Data Validation

- Always validate data with Zod schemas
- Sanitize user inputs
- Implement proper error handling
- Validate file uploads
- Check data types and formats

## API Security

- Use HTTPS for all API calls
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Validate all API responses
- Use API rate limiting
- Implement request size limits

## Environment Variables

- Never commit sensitive data
- Use proper environment variable naming
- Implement proper secret management
- Use different secrets for different environments
- Rotate secrets regularly

## XSS Prevention

- Sanitize user-generated content
- Use proper HTML escaping
- Implement Content Security Policy (CSP)
- Use React's built-in XSS protection
- Validate and sanitize URLs

## CSRF Protection

- Use CSRF tokens for state-changing operations
- Implement proper token validation
- Use SameSite cookie attributes
- Validate request origins

## Input Sanitization

```typescript
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

// Sanitize HTML content
function sanitizeHtml(html: string): string {
  return DOMPurify.sanitize(html);
}

// Validate file uploads
function validateFile(file: File): boolean {
  const allowedTypes = ['image/jpeg', 'image/png', 'image/webp'];
  const maxSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5MB

  return allowedTypes.includes(file.type) && file.size <= maxSize;
}
```

## API Security Patterns

```typescript
// Rate limiting middleware
const rateLimit = {
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100, // limit each IP to 100 requests per windowMs
};

// Input validation
function validateInput(data: unknown) {
  const schema = z.object({
    title: z.string().min(1).max(100),
    content: z.string().min(1).max(10000),
    tags: z.array(z.string()).max(10),
  });

  return schema.parse(data);
}
```

## Secure Headers

```typescript
// Security headers configuration
const securityHeaders = {
  'Content-Security-Policy': "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'",
  'X-Frame-Options': 'DENY',
  'X-Content-Type-Options': 'nosniff',
  'Referrer-Policy': 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin',
  'Permissions-Policy': 'camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()',
};
```

## Password Security

- Use strong password requirements
- Implement password hashing (bcrypt)
- Use salt for password hashing
- Implement password reset functionality
- Store passwords securely

## Session Management

- Use secure session cookies
- Implement session timeout
- Invalidate sessions on logout
- Use secure session storage
- Implement session regeneration

## Error Handling

- Don't expose sensitive information in errors
- Log errors securely
- Use generic error messages for users
- Implement proper error boundaries

## File Upload Security

- Validate file types and sizes
- Scan uploaded files for malware
- Store files securely
- Use secure file serving
- Implement file access controls

## Database Security

- Use parameterized queries
- Implement proper access controls
- Encrypt sensitive data
- Use connection pooling
- Implement database backups

## Monitoring and Logging

- Log security events
- Monitor for suspicious activity
- Implement intrusion detection
- Track failed login attempts
- Monitor API usage patterns

